WEBVTT

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.320
Type seven dangerous lifeforms.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.900
Everything has been thrown into chaos because of them.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.530
Including your plan to liberate Dorssia?

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:18.460
Due to your background, I was once asked by Captain Cain to investigate you behind your back.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.540
<i>Rejoice, H-Neun.</i>

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.790
<i>X-Eins's body will soon belong to my comrade.</i>

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.400
<i>You bastard!</i>

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.050
<i>We should sound the gun salute.</i>

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.760
Is that...

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:41.270
Impossible!

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.980
But true. It was Captain Cain who killed H-Neun.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.360
I want to avenge H-Neun...

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.010
I want to avenge my friend.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.070
It's too much for them!

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.710
We'll be okay! Don't give up!

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:06.940
Aw, shit!

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.260
Carmilla?!

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.730
It's Unit 4!

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.260
Rukino's back!

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.120
We're gonna make it!

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:25.890
We're saved!

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.820
They say that Unit 4's back!

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.400
I hear Tokishima's with her.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.820
Haruto? He's back?

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.230
Looks like we made it back just in time.

00:01:35.230 --> 00:01:37.290
Yeah. And now...

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.240
Wow, this thing really took a beating.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.910
That's not surprising, after fighting a Valvrave.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.680
Hey, are you okay?

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.350
I've got a survivor here!

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:53.050
Send some people over! Let's get the pilot out of there!

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:30.980
I want to create a country where humans and holy spirits can live together.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:34.360
And to do that, we need a place to settle, huh?

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.360
Hey, it's going to take more than land to make that work, you know?

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.610
We'll do things one step at a time! It's all we can do right now.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.380
Well, still. It's just not feasible with only four Valvraves.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:46.910
Module 77 is being guarded by 40,000 allied forces soldiers.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.290
I'll go.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:52.540
Don't get swept up in the excitement. Think it through carefully, and—

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:55.540
I want a place where I can belong, too.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.300
Akira...

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.760
We can win.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.670
L-Elf has already begun infiltrating them.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.180
A simultaneous attack from inside and outside.

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.720
Between us and L-Elf, this plan will work.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.760
We can trust you, right?

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:09.600
Of course.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:11.400
You can count on me.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.730
I'll get our home back no matter what.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:27.740
Switching places with an injured soldier to infiltrate an enemy position.

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.210
That's the same gambit you used in the New Guinea Conflict.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:35.630
You weren't the one who gave me this.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.060
Why didn't you say anything?

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.920
If I had, would you have believed me?

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:46.690
I no longer bear you any ill will.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.930
That said, you are an enemy of the state.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.940
However, my beloved homeland is being

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:56.440
gradually consumed in secret by monsters.

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:01.570
And so, L-Elf, I want you to assist us with our mission.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.570
Mission objectives?

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:07.990
The elimination of Captain Cain and all parties related to him.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.720
Our interests are aligned, I see.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:14.280
I hereby sanction Special Forces Lieutenant L-Elf's return to duty.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.770
Blitzendegen.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:25.590
So, how much do you remember?

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:29.880
I asked Professor Kibukawa about the runes.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:32.660
Our memories will fade away, right?

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.480
And in the end, we...

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:39.070
Everything's fine! I can still remember everything just fine.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.230
There's nothing to worry about.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.380
Don't put on a tough act, not to me.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:45.900
Your "We'll win for sure" speech back there was also to put everyone at ease, right?

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.380
Sometimes you have to put on a brave face.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:53.290
For others and for yourself.

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:54.640
Haruto...

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.500
Let's make a deal.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:05:59.190
Neither of us gives up to the bitter end.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:03.110
<i>If I don't give up,</i>

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.160
<i>will he also see how I feel?</i>

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:06.760
What?

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:09.640
Forget it. It's nothing.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:14.470
I have no idea what the outcome will be, but if we give up, it'll never happen.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.070
Deal.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.400
I'm borrowing this, Inuzuka.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:27.400
You always slack off when it comes to defense, Yamada. You need it.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:31.160
It ain't a problem! I punch them before they can punch me.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:34.970
And for the last time: it's "Thunder", damn it!

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:39.500
Put some effort into defense, okay?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.690
Get off my case, man!

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:43.250
We're talking tens of thousands of enemies!

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.950
I'm not sure if even the Valvraves can win against that many, so—

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:46.880
My glasses...

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.640
Don't worry about me! I'm coming back!

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.680
After all, I got new mates now, right?

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:04.650
Thanks.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:05.920
Is that enough?

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:06.650
Yeah.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:08.320
You sure?

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:10.860
Um...

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:12.940
It's okay, Akira.

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.510
Eat me if you want!

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.790
Akira! I shouldn't have said that!

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:22.580
Akira!

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:25.430
You're such a jerk.

00:07:26.870 --> 00:07:31.340
In regards to the disposal of the holy spirits, the Council supports your plan.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:36.470
I am of the school of thought that surprise attacks should be as sensational as possible.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:41.540
Thanks to your plan, the public has
directed their rage at those students.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:47.980
Prue, this will make it easier to retrieve your sister.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.680
We never would have known of those artificial Magius

00:07:55.680 --> 00:07:59.080
if you had not informed us of the Valvrave Project.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:00.250
You have our gratitude.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.920
You have mine as well, Cain.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.890
You rescued me when I was lost and adrift.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:17.390
I'm sorry, Sashinami. I'm supposed to be the adult here, but...

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:20.180
Don't say that. Just get some rest.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.640
Tokishima Haruto is coming!

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.350
He's asking for permission to land. What do you want us to do?

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:26.830
He's come for revenge!

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:28.440
After what we did, can you blame him?

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:29.860
Turn him away, Shoko.

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:31.900
But without the Valvraves to protect us, we're as good as—

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:33.550
You've got to do something, Sashinami!

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.180
You're the Prime Minister, aren't you?

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:45.420
It's Haruto!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.290
He's alive!

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:48.140
I knew it! He really is a monster!

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:49.060
Why's he here?

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:50.770
This is a ship for humans, dude!

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:51.950
Murderer!

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:53.770
Shoko, I...

00:08:53.770 --> 00:08:58.100
You have our thanks for saving us all from the allied forces.

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:03.230
That said, please restrict yourself to this hangar.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:09.150
As Prime Minister, I can't let you in, not when I can't be certain you are not a threat.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.350
I shouldn't have lied to you...

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:26.290
If I'd been honest with you, even if it meant getting hurt,

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:31.550
maybe we could've found a way to work through this together.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:35.190
With that in mind,

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:37.390
I'm at least

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:40.510
going to unveil the world to you.

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:46.310
Unveil the world?

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.190
I don't get humans at all.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.270
You don't?

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:52.970
That human was sitting in here for ages, crying.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:56.450
Saying, "I'm sorry, Haruto. I'm sorry."

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:14.550
Sometimes you have to put on a brave face.

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:30.490
Why can't we catch a break?

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:58.380
Citizens of the world! This is a historic day!

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:03.510
On that fateful day, our two countries, which could not be said to have ever been on friendly terms,

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:09.390
have joined together in common cause to exterminate the shared enemy of all mankind!

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.190
The nerve of him, making us out to be the bad guys!

00:11:12.190 --> 00:11:16.320
The key to making people get along is to have a common enemy.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.510
Was it a good idea to let them go?

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:23.740
We decided to trust them and wait, didn't we? They said that if we went, we'd only get in the way.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:24.730
It's all right.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.760
They'll be back. I know they will be.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:37.300
Enemy contact! Valvraves, four of them!

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.050
So they've come.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:46.310
Harakiri Blade complete. Let's move in and engage them up close.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:52.310
Proceed according to plan. Deliver Unit 6 to satellite Nice 052 by 1950!

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:56.820
We're here to act as her shield and cut a path through these guys!

00:11:59.180 --> 00:12:03.450
Inuzuka, I'm gonna need your help on this one.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:58.870
They're falling back?

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:02.400
Hit and away... They're biding their time?

00:13:02.400 --> 00:13:05.220
They know our weakness all too well.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.980
The Ardor Grips seem to be doing the trick.

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:20.480
They're letting us fight without having to worry as much about heat management, but still...

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:23.720
Deploying in depth defense formation per your orders, Captain!

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:25.490
Waiting for Valvrave thermal runaway!

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.930
This plan of theirs is reckless beyond belief.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:30.330
They can't possibly break through with just four units.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:31.640
I suppose not.

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:34.220
I'll let you handle this.

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:34.970
Captain?

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:36.750
Million to one shots do happen.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:41.750
Besides, I want to dispatch Unit 1 personally.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.040
Message from A-Drei's Kirschbaum.

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:50.730
He says they are leaving to assist in the defense of Module 77.

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:54.260
It's working. Inform the escort ships in the front and at the harbor.

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:58.440
Three Valvraves are breaching defensive perimeter number eight!

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.520
Is the Kirschbaum squadron on its way?

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.790
Haruto! Be careful! You're leaking runes!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.310
What? But I...

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.340
Shoko...

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:24.250
Shoko!

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.560
Oh shit!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:43.110
Haruto!

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.310
They have that many humanoid types?

00:14:51.310 --> 00:14:53.490
Leave them to me. I'll scatter them!

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:00.960
The rest of you, go on ahead!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:03.210
Don't! We have to fight together!

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:07.970
We made a deal to never give up, remember? I'm going with our best bet!

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:12.180
Understood. I'll leave you some Impact Boosters!

00:15:16.610 --> 00:15:18.070
Thanks, Haruto.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:25.570
I know that you guys can't use that attack in quick succession!

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:27.360
Now you're stuck!

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.860
A second line?!

00:15:46.510 --> 00:15:48.260
Valvrave Green is disengaging!

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.760
It has withdrawn at attack speed 14!

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:52.920
<i>So this was too big a risk after all?</i>

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:10.820
We'll enter the sea.

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:13.660
Keep going in that direction, and it will take us to the heart of Module 77.

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:15.280
I know.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:31.920
Our analysis has determined that they are military weapons artificially created by the leaders of the old JIOR.

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:37.300
There was likely a spirit of patriotism in the environment that gave rise to such monsters.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:40.110
But make no mistake!

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:46.560
We must place the love of humanity as a whole above the love of any one state!

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:52.690
Our scientific ability progressed too far and created those monsters!

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.700
Aren't Haruto and the others there yet?

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:55.950
They aren't showing anything about the battle on TV...

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:55.950
They can only be described as a threat—

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:01.660
Shoko!

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:09.880
I don't want to forget. I don't want to forget her!

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:17.800
But I'm going to fight anyway!

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:27.400
Because if we run and hide, there's no future for us!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:32.860
L-Elf!

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.310
Nice 052!

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:11.700
I'm latched on!

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:17.320
Now I can—

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:19.870
You're finally here!

00:18:29.870 --> 00:18:30.670
Yamada?!

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:34.770
Your shield!

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:39.050
Don't worry about that! Just concentrate! Nobody but you can do this job!

00:18:39.520 --> 00:18:40.600
Yamada...

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:53.860
Inuzuka, you better keep Akira safe, ya hear?

00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:06.160
Hey, you're good! I'm having a blast!

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:17.050
I don't regret becoming a holy spirit! Not one damn bit!

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:20.810
I was able to get my revenge and keep my friends safe!

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:22.760
It's the fucking best!

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.350
Akira! Hurry!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.850
They have ARUS Splicers, too?!

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.740
You're dead!

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:47.740
Sucker.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:52.420
Yamada!

00:19:52.840 --> 00:19:54.040
We're done here!

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:11.350
Hacking successful! I did it! I did it, Yamada!

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:18.780
Yamada? Y-Yamada!

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:21.150
<i>No! Yamada!</i>

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:23.110
I can hear you...

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:28.540
You pulled it off, huh? Good deal...

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.060
See ya around, Akira.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:38.170
My mate Nobu was gettin' lonely, see...

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:46.180
Put some effort into defense, huh?

00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:51.810
I guess you were right about that, Otamaya...

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:58.440
Yamada!

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:04.780
L-Elf!

00:21:39.430 --> 00:21:40.500
He did it!

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:41.480
Now they'll see!

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:57.550
The wound!

00:21:57.550 --> 00:21:59.050
It healed!

00:21:59.870 --> 00:22:02.540
This can't be happening! Stop the broadcast!

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:04.800
What are you doing?! Hurry, have them cut the transmission!

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:08.670
It's no use! The communications satellite has been hacked!

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:10.180
We can't control it!

00:22:11.570 --> 00:22:13.930
So that's what the Valvraves were doing!

00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:15.930
I'll defend this transmission with my life!

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:19.190
Spread! Spread!

00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:15.430
PREVIEW

00:24:13.720 --> 00:24:18.970
Next time, Episode 24: Liberation Towards Tomorrow.

00:24:19.970 --> 00:24:25.480
Valvrave the Liberator... The system that unveils the world.

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:27.480
EPISODE 24

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:27.480
Liberation Towards Tomorrow
